{"content_hash": "eab14c8b09303cbe", "version_id": 192, "article_id": 20, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies at 102", "title_zh": "奥斯卡影后伊娃·玛丽·森特去世，享年102岁", "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqze43ky1xgdo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/98d6/live/7a402d70-c229-11f1-babe-4199b0e7ccea.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 214, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "Eva Marie Saint was a famous Hollywood actress. She won an Oscar and acted in many classic films. She died at home in Los Angeles at the age of 102.", "lead_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·森特是好莱坞著名女演员。她拿过奥斯卡奖，演过很多经典电影。她在洛杉矶家中去世，享年102岁。", "preview": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family said she died of natural causes, with her love", "preview_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·森特于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人说她是自然死亡，去世时亲人都在身边。直到去世前，她一直是健在的奥斯卡得主中年纪最大的一位。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 182, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/audio/20/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 89.875, "size_bytes": 543024, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 254, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/data/versions/192.json", "paragraphs": ["Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family said she died of natural causes, with her loved ones around her. Until her death, she was the oldest living Oscar winner.", "Saint won an Oscar for her first film, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle, a kind and strong woman. Five years later, she starred in Alfred Hitchcock's North by Northwest. She played a beautiful and dangerous spy.", "Saint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. But she loved theatre and moved to New York to study acting. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s. Later, she won an Emmy Award in 1990.", "Saint acted with many famous stars, like Marlon Brando and Cary Grant. She stopped acting for a while to raise her family. In 2006, she returned to the big screen in Superman Returns. She played Clark Kent's mother. She was in her 80s then.", "Saint said that getting older made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. She was married to director Jeffrey Hayden for 65 years. He died in 2016. She leaves behind two children."], "paragraphs_zh": ["伊娃·玛丽·森特于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人说她是自然死亡，去世时亲人都在身边。直到去世前，她一直是健在的奥斯卡得主中年纪最大的一位。", "1954年，森特凭借自己的第一部电影《码头风云》获得奥斯卡奖。她在片中饰演伊迪·多伊尔，一个善良而坚强的女人。五年后，她主演了阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的《西北偏北》，扮演一个美丽又危险的女间谍。", "森特1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克。她最初想当老师，但后来爱上了戏剧，便搬到纽约学习表演。20世纪40年代末，她从电视直播开始自己的演艺生涯。1990年，她获得了艾美奖。", "森特曾与许多著名影星合作，比如马龙·白兰度和加里·格兰特。她曾一度停止演戏，专心照顾家庭。2006年，她重返大银幕，出演《超人归来》，扮演克拉克·肯特的母亲。那时她已经80多岁了。", "森特说，年龄的增长让她成为更好的演员。她告诉特纳经典电影频道：“你活得越久，就越聪明。”她与导演杰弗里·海登结婚65年，海登于2016年去世。她身后留下两个孩子。"], "body": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family said she died of natural causes, with her loved ones around her. Until her death, she was the oldest living Oscar winner.\n\nSaint won an Oscar for her first film, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle, a kind and strong woman. Five years later, she starred in Alfred Hitchcock's North by Northwest. She played a beautiful and dangerous spy.\n\nSaint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. But she loved theatre and moved to New York to study acting. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s. Later, she won an Emmy Award in 1990.\n\nSaint acted with many famous stars, like Marlon Brando and Cary Grant. She stopped acting for a while to raise her family. In 2006, she returned to the big screen in Superman Returns. She played Clark Kent's mother. She was in her 80s then.\n\nSaint said that getting older made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. She was married to director Jeffrey Hayden for 65 years. He died in 2016. She leaves behind two children.", "body_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·森特于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人说她是自然死亡，去世时亲人都在身边。直到去世前，她一直是健在的奥斯卡得主中年纪最大的一位。\n\n1954年，森特凭借自己的第一部电影《码头风云》获得奥斯卡奖。她在片中饰演伊迪·多伊尔，一个善良而坚强的女人。五年后，她主演了阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的《西北偏北》，扮演一个美丽又危险的女间谍。\n\n森特1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克。她最初想当老师，但后来爱上了戏剧，便搬到纽约学习表演。20世纪40年代末，她从电视直播开始自己的演艺生涯。1990年，她获得了艾美奖。\n\n森特曾与许多著名影星合作，比如马龙·白兰度和加里·格兰特。她曾一度停止演戏，专心照顾家庭。2006年，她重返大银幕，出演《超人归来》，扮演克拉克·肯特的母亲。那时她已经80多岁了。\n\n森特说，年龄的增长让她成为更好的演员。她告诉特纳经典电影频道：“你活得越久，就越聪明。”她与导演杰弗里·海登结婚65年，海登于2016年去世。她身后留下两个孩子。", "text": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family said she died of natural causes, with her loved ones around her. Until her death, she was the oldest living Oscar winner. Saint won an Oscar for her first film, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle, a kind and strong woman. Five years later, she starred in Alfred Hitchcock's North by Northwest. She played a beautiful and dangerous spy. Saint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. But she loved theatre and moved to New York to study acting. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s. Later, she won an Emmy Award in 1990. Saint acted with many famous stars, like Marlon Brando and Cary Grant. She stopped acting for a while to raise her family. In 2006, she returned to the big screen in Superman Returns. She played Clark Kent's mother. She was in her 80s then. Saint said that getting older made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. She was married to director Jeffrey Hayden for 65 years. He died in 2016. She leaves behind two children.", "vocab": [{"word": "actress", "pos": "noun", "zh": "女演员", "note": "male: actor"}, {"word": "Oscar", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奥斯卡奖", "note": "美国电影最高奖"}, {"word": "film", "pos": "noun", "zh": "电影", "note": "同 movie"}, {"word": "star", "pos": "verb", "zh": "主演", "note": "star in a film"}, {"word": "die", "pos": "verb", "zh": "去世", "note": "过去式 died"}, {"word": "born", "pos": "adj", "zh": "出生的", "note": "be born in + 地点/年份"}, {"word": "career", "pos": "noun", "zh": "职业生涯", "note": ""}, {"word": "raise a family", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "养家，抚养孩子", "note": ""}], "title_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102", "summary_original": "She starred opposite Marlon Brando in On the Waterfront, then alongside Cary Grant in Hitchcock's North by Northwest.", "body_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102\nBy\nPaul Glynn\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n7 October 2026\nEva Marie Saint, the Oscar-winning actress who starred in Hollywood classics such as On the Waterfront and North by Northwest, has died aged 102.\nSaint won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in director Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama, On the Waterfront; playing Edie Doyle, the moral compass of the film and love interest of Marlon Brando's conflicted boxer-turned-docker.\nFive years later, she portrayed femme fatale Eve Kendall, dangerously seducing Cary Grant's entangled advertising executive in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller, North by Northwest.\nShe died on Tuesday of natural causes, surrounded by family and loved ones at her home in Los Angeles, family representative Jeff Sanderson confirmed.\nUntil her death, Saint was the oldest surviving Oscar winner and one of the last remaining stars of Hollywood's golden age.\nStarting her career in live television in the late 1940s, she also won an Emmy Award in 1990 for her career-capping role as the rich widow Lil Van Degan Altemus in People Like Us.\nBorn in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had originally intended to become a teacher before developing a passion for theatre.\nShe trained in New York at the Herbert Berghof Studio and then the Actors Studio - the home of method acting - co-founded by Kazan.\nSaint burst on to the Hollywood scene with her performance as the gentle but resolute Edie in Kazan's classic, On the Waterfront.\nHer co-star Brando was an intense method actor and Saint admitted to having found him \"adorable\" but \"a little frightening\".\n\"I felt that he could see right through me,\" she told Turner Classic Movies (TCM) in a 2013 interview.\nAccepting her Oscar trophy while nine-months pregnant, Saint quipped: \"I may have the baby right here!\".\nShe wasn't far off, having her son just two days afterwards.\nShe was considered a surprise choice, though, to play one of Hitchcock's cool and calculating heroines in his masterpiece, North by Northwest.\nThe English filmmaker was known for being very demanding of his leading ladies.\n\"He worked with me from the outside in,\" said Saint.\n\"My hair, my makeup, my shoes, my jewellery, my purse, my gloves, everything. And just from creating that exterior for me, he gave me the sense of a spy lady.\"\nCritics have argued that her character helped to create the sophisticated, sexually confident and intelligent blonde-haired archetype that many \"Bond women\", as they have been known, later followed in the 007 films.\nSaint also starred opposite Paul Newman in Otto Preminger's Exodus in 1960, and alongside Warren Beatty in John Frankenheimer's All Fall Down.\nBut she then scaled back her career while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden.\nHalf a century later, Saint made a big screen comeback as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in the 2006 blockbuster Superman Returns, while in her 80s.\nAnd she later had parts in the supernatural fantasy Winter's Tale, alongside Colin Farrell and Russell Crowe, and the 2019 nun drama Mariette in Ecstasy.\nThis all followed her Emmy win in 1990 for her role in the TV miniseries People Like Us, which was set among New York's high society.\nSaint, who has two stars on the Hollywood Walk of Fame for her movie and TV work, said her longevity in acting had given her work extra depth.\n\"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told TCM.\n\"You've gone through different emotional experiences in your own life, and hopefully, you understand things better.\n\"And that makes you a better actress.\"\nSaint's marriage to Hayden lasted for 65 years, until his death in 2016, and she is survived by their two children.\nRelated topics\nActing\nFilm\nTelevision\nMore on this story\nParamount takes over Warner Bros in $110bn Hollywood merger\nPublished\n1 day ago\nAmazon wins global rights to stream Emmys in six-year deal\nPublished\n1 day ago\nOscars ceremony moving to new home outside Hollywood\nPublished\n26 March", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:14:34.129895", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Eva", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.387, "sm": 100, "em": 387, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Marie", "s": 0.4, "e": 0.775, "sm": 400, "em": 775, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "Saint", "s": 0.787, "e": 1.075, "sm": 787, "em": 1075, "cs": 10, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "died", "s": 1.087, "e": 1.362, "sm": 1087, "em": 1362, "cs": 16, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "on", "s": 1.375, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1375, "em": 1525, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Tuesday", "s": 1.538, "e": 2.038, "sm": 1537, "em": 2037, "cs": 24, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "at", "s": 2.05, "e": 2.162, "sm": 2050, "em": 2162, "cs": 32, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "her", "s": 2.175, "e": 2.312, "sm": 2175, "em": 2312, "cs": 35, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "home", "s": 2.325, "e": 2.613, "sm": 2325, "em": 2612, "cs": 39, "ce": 43, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "in", "s": 2.625, "e": 2.737, "sm": 2625, "em": 2737, "cs": 44, "ce": 46, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "Los", "s": 2.75, "e": 3.0, "sm": 2750, "em": 3000, 